The draft proposes retaining eleven earlier disjoint held-out controls and
adding a newly constructed tuning case, a supplementary held-out and four
ordered reserves. Its static graph and metadata checks do not establish actual
public lowering, canonical owner independence, recorded campaign coverage,
reduction success, performance, or eligibility for a final cache profile.
Those remain separate acceptance steps. The earlier tuning case and overlapping
held-out remain immutable known-seen controls; this capsule changes no old input,
role, receipt, expectation, benchmark or cache.

The archive has five regular members: the three exact original files, a source
manifest and checksums. References to historical metadata are only references;
no runtime reports, active configuration, PID, registration ticket, scientific
payload, executable, cache, license value or environment file is included.
Two archive passes are byte-identical; safe normalized paths and member hashes
were checked, and Python source was parsed without importing or executing it.
This note was compiled with existing Typst. No new design, test case, Native job,
measurement, cache selection or freeze was performed to produce the capsule.

Extracting this historical draft authorizes nothing. Any future accepted suite
must receive its own explicit freeze and authenticated qualification, preserving
this draft and all earlier evidence rather than relabeling them as accepted.
